Here's Title at **1 s**, halfway through its first move. The faint "An easing lesson" text in the middle should be Title (I couldn't get its exact position from AE). It's still fading in here, because its Position, Scale and Opacity all animate from 0.5 s to 1.5 s.

At the moment every one of those moves runs at a **constant speed**. Title starts at full speed at 0.5 s and stops dead at 1.5 s. Real objects don't move like that, so it looks mechanical. **Easing** makes the motion speed up gently out of a keyframe and slow down gently into the next one.

**How to do it:**
1. Select Title and press **U** to show its keyframes.
2. Select the keys of a pair, then choose **Animation > Keyframe Assistant > Easy Ease** (or press **F9**).
3. The diamond keyframe icons turn into hourglass shapes. Open the **Graph Editor** to check: the speed curve should rise and fall smoothly instead of being flat with hard corners.

**Your pairs on Title:**
- Position, 0.5 s → 1.5 s
- Position, 1.5 s → 3 s
- Scale, 0.5 s → 1.5 s
- Opacity, 0.5 s → 1.5 s

